WEBVTT

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.240
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.240
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:24.290
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:24.290
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.060
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.060
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.060
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.060
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:51.280
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:51.280
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:01.870
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:01.870
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.670
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.670
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.670
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.670
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.760
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.760
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.640
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.640
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:34.280
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:34.280
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.500
<i>Koshiro!</i>

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.170
<i>Koshiro, you have to do this!</i>

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.890
<i>The mysterious world where Digimon live,
the Digital World.</i>

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.250
<i>Taichi Yagami and the Chosen Ones
with their partner Digimon</i>

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.860
<i>continue their adventure.</i>

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:23.160
<i>The hands of evil that target
the energy born from internet confusion</i>

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:28.160
<i>caused the International
Space Station to fall.</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.880
<i>The estimated point of impact is Tokyo.</i>

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.230
<i>The ISS draws near.</i>

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.510
<i>The only ones who can stop it is...</i>

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.100
Don't we know the specific
point of impact yet?!

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.440
Not yet! We can't
calculate its trajectory!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.990
<i>This is Moscow.</i>

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:00.550
<i>Houston, where's the command
to shift the trajectory?!</i>

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:03.680
It's too late!
We cannot shift it at this point!

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.180
<i>This is Tsukuba.
The thermal control system won't work.</i>

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.410
<i>At this rate, there's a chance
the station may explode.</i>

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:15.040
We know that already! We don't even know
where in Tokyo it's going to fall.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.800
Every control system has failed to work.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>All we can do now is pray.</i>

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.890
Hey!

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.480
OPERATION SATELLITE SNIPER

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.030
Koshiro, what's that?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.050
Wow... amazing.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.540
Digimon fossils?

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.390
They're probably ancient Digimon.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:59.980
They were so big they didn't disappear
completely and remained as fossils.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.940
Wonder what Digimon they were.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.180
They won't suddenly start moving, right?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.180
It kind of looks like they fought
and ended up in a draw.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.750
Does this have something to do with
the ancient battle with Millenniumon too?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.870
No.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:23.150
Digimon's battles in the Digital World
are not only between light and dark.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:31.120
The law of nature, fight for survival,
and there's also battles over pride.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.960
I think what's important now
is that pillar of light.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.190
The tremendous energy produced
by the clash between those two Digimon

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:49.030
pierced the heavens
and even distorted space.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:53.930
Even now, after countless years,
its effects have continued to remain.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.360
Koshiro-san has done an awful load
of research since he got here!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.990
So, what's at the top of that light?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:06.610
Right! That's the most important point!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.120
The top of that pillar of light
is basically a singularity.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.850
It's outside of this Digital World
where the world of the Network is exposed.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:22.050
From there, we should be able to
interact with our world.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.550
Interact?

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:29.820
It means we can do a lot of things to
the human world from this Digital World.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.060
And we use that...

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.810
...to change the ISS's trajectory
from within the Network.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.110
<i>Yes, just like how we stopped
Tokyo's missile crash.</i>

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.160
That's quite a rough plan.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.800
But how are we actually gonna do that?

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.950
During the missile crisis,
I don't really remember what I did.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.210
Data distorted by Digimon's power...

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.080
will be corrected by Digimon's power!

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:09.090
We're going to snipe the ISS control point
inside the Network at a precise angle.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:15.640
We may be able to shift its path toward
the ocean without destroying the ISS.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.190
What's "snipe"?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:21.250
It means to target and shoot.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.460
So we're not gonna destroy it,
we're gonna divert it.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.950
Yes. If we succeed, there'll be no worry
of debris falling onto the city.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.070
So there'll be no damage on Tokyo!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.830
That's amazing! Koshiro, you're awesome!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.350
But we have only one chance.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:41.600
Even if it's calculated,
we must shoot it accurately.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:45.360
And I haven't worked out
several uncertainties either.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.420
There's no guarantee it'll actually work.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:51.470
So it's a huge gamble then.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:57.220
Honestly, if we can get closer,
it would be more accurate...

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:02.480
but there's only 20 minutes left until
the ISS passes through the snipe point.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.610
Only a little left.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.860
Twenty minutes, huh...

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.880
That's more than enough!

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.700
What?

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.120
Yeah!

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.070
Let's go!

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.040
Agumon Evolution!

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.250
Greymon!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.670
Taichi-san!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:31.190
You don't know until you try, right?

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:32.680
R-Right.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.010
There's no time. Let's go!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.220
A-All right, I will support you!

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:46.570
Greymon Super Evolution!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.490
Metalgreymon!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.930
Piyomon Evolution!

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:57.300
Tentomon Evolution!

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:58.990
Patamon Evolution!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.000
Birdramon!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.750
Kabuterimon!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.460
Pegasmon!

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.210
How much time's left?!

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.720
Fifteen minutes!

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.600
Commence operation!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.960
<i>Moments earlier,
the evacuation order has expanded</i>

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.400
<i>from the 23 wards to all of Tokyo.</i>

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.300
<i>If any senior citizens
live alone near you,</i>

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:35.990
<i>please assist them and evacuate
as soon as possible.</i>

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.510
Just reaching the top
will be cutting it close!

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:41.750
Let's hurry!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.040
Okay!

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.670
Don't worry, I'm with you!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.800
Is the lightning targeting us?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.600
Pegasmon!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.940
Shooting Star!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:16.860
What's that?!

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.990
That's... Bladekuwagamon!

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:25.710
Bladekuwagamon?

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.250
BLADEKUWAGAMON

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.310
Lightning doesn't bother them.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:36.220
That form is probably an evolution
fit for this environment.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:41.350
You must be nuts
to want to live in a place like this!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:44.870
This light is a concentration of energy.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:48.350
If you're immune to lightning,
it's a perfect feeding ground!

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:53.730
Metalgreymon!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.240
We've been identified as enemies!
Be careful!

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.490
Meteor Wing!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.310
Birdramon!

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.380
I-I'm fine!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.460
You...

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.220
They're hard!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.270
They're coming! Kabuterimon!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.400
Let's do this!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:40.450
Kabuterimon Super Evolution!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.410
Atlurkabuterimon!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.790
Birdramon Super Evolution!

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.500
Garudamon!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.650
I'll beat them up!

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:00.880
Horn Buster!

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.600
Shadow Wing!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.270
Higher!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.320
Just a little farther until the very top!

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.570
How much time's left?!

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.160
<i>Eight minutes!</i>

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.040
Good, we can still make it!

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.420
Let's go, Koshiro!

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.420
Y-Yes!

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:41.760
Tailmon?

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.550
Something's coming again!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:44.970
Huh?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.080
What was that attack?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.580
That!

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.430
What's that?!

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:27.430
Looks like Bladekuwagamon's boss!

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.060
Metallifekuwagamon, an Ultimate Digimon!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.890
METALLIFEKUWAGAMON

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.320
The lasers are following us!

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.830
Jeez, what is all this?!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:56.890
Tailmon!

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.080
Got it!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.590
Neko Kick!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.590
Neko Scratch!

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.100
Leave this to us!

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.480
Taichi-san, you guys go on ahead!

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.980
I'm counting on you, Takeru!

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:31.200
Six minutes left!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.580
Just a little further till the very top!

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.660
Shadow Wing!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:25.800
Garudamon!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.090
Sora!

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:31.590
Don't worry!

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.220
There's no time! Go!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.270
Let's go, Koshiro!

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.410
Koshiro!

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.540
Four minutes left!

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.060
The reconnaissance satellite's
footage is in!

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.680
Put it on the main monitor!

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.080
What's the altitude?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.980
Approximately 16,000 feet.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:21.640
<i>It's still falling!</i>

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:51.800
We're not giving up!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.760
Taichi-san, Metalgreymon?!

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.980
Metalgreymon...

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.730
Mega Evolution!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.070
Blitzgreymon!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.240
BLITZGREYMON

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.040
Blitzgreymon...

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.200
What's this evolution?!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.750
Could it be...

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.290
Elec Guard!

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:33.510
Metalgreymon's evolution that adapted
to this environment...

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:37.430
That's this form, Blitzgreymon!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:42.600
What?! That is mighty brilliant...
Blitzgreymon!

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.900
Plasma Stake!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:17.610
Koshiro!

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.850
We'll take all these guys.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.270
What?

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.890
Koshiro, you have to do this!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.810
Me?!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:32.190
No way! I can support you, but I can't--

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.440
Koshiro!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.740
I leave it to you!

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.490
Taichi-san...

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.410
I'm counting on you!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.000
Yes!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.590
Go, Koshiro!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.170
Thunder Vernier!

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:14.440
I have to do this alone...

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.490
No, that's wrong.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.790
<i>"I like being alone."</i>

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:31.040
<i>I used to say that all the time to people.</i>

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.670
<i>I was always observing everyone
in the corner of the class.</i>

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.030
<i>Even when grown-ups were worried,</i>

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:41.840
<i>I never cared,
thinking I was better-off being alone.</i>

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:50.160
<i>But now, I have you, Atlurkabuterimon.</i>

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.520
<i>And...</i>

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:54.000
Thanks, Koshiro.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.190
Huh? I didn't do anything.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:00.170
You looked everything up and informed us.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:02.090
And supported us.

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:03.830
You really saved us all.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>You're seriously awesome, Koshiro.</i>

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.340
<i>I have everyone.</i>

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.490
That's why I gotta do it!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.270
For everyone, we'll do it!

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:31.540
That's it, Koshiro-san!
This is our moment!

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:35.020
The biggest stage of our lives!

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.480
Atlurkabuterimon! Prepare to shoot!

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.950
<i>Until the executable snipe point...
eight seconds!</i>

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.000
Horn...

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.300
Now!

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.760
...Buster!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.960
What happened?!

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:26.840
Unbelievable... It seems
the ISS's trajectory has changed!

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.490
The cause is unclear.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.510
Yes!

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:53.350
Alright! We did it, Koshiro-san!

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.920
<i>Now, an announcement
from the Ministry of Defense.</i>

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:09.530
<i>The International Space Station,
which was said to fall into the city,</i>

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:14.270
<i>suddenly changed its trajectory
1,000 meters above Odaiba earlier.</i>

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:17.230
<i>And its fall into Tokyo Bay
has been confirmed.</i>

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:20.020
<i>There are no casualties identified.</i>

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.360
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:25.880
<i>The International Space Station,
which was said to fall into the city...</i>

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:32.870
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:35.890
<i>Blitzgreymon.</i>

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:38.770
<i>This Digimon is a subspecies
of Wargreymon.</i>

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.710
LEVEL: MEGA

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:43.340
<i>Blitzgreymon protects allies
with a shield made of plasma particles.</i>

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:41.040
TYPE: CYBORG

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.340
SPECIAL MOVE: PLASMA STAKE
THUNDER VERNIER / ELEC GUARD

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:45.230
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:48.690
<i>Blitzgreymon has mega evolved
into a very cool form.</i>

00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:53.260
<i>Since then, Tentomon has kept mumbling,
"That is mighty brilliant."</i>

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.100
<i>One day, you too...</i>

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:59.980
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:23:01.850 --> 00:23:05.710
<i>When Gogmamon repels attacks
with a gemstone body,</i>

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:08.400
<i>Mimi unleashes her ultimate, secret plan.</i>

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:11.670
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"Mimi-chan Wars"</i>

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:14.490
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
